  "releaseNotes": "- PermissionField: new IsExcludeMode property inverts the meaning of TargetFields to \"all fields except the specified ones\". Intended for whole-record locks such as approval flows (\"everything read-only except the comment while approving\"); fields added to the module later are covered automatically (fail-closed). Id, OptimisticLocking, and permission fields themselves are always excluded implicitly. The design check skips the \"cannot be a target\" report in exclude mode (listing such fields is harmless) and evaluates the ExecuteSqlField row-data-condition report against the effective target set.",
